{"awe":{"id":"dd7d3516-9355-46c8-a558-2ccbe73a6628","word":"awe","trans":[{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"feeling of fear and reverence","tags":["masculine"],"word":"temor"},{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"feeling of amazement","tags":["masculine"],"word":"espanto"},{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"feeling of amazement","tags":["feminine"],"word":"admiração"}],"pos":"noun","tags":null,"senses":[{"examples":[{"text":"Last spring, the periodical cicadas emerged across eastern North America. Their vast numbers and short above-ground life spans inspired awe and irritation in humans—and made for good meals for birds and small mammals.","ref":"2012 March-April, Anna Lena Phillips, “Sneaky Silk Moths”, in American Scientist, volume 100, number 2, archived from the original on 19 Feb 2013, page 172:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[136,139]],"id":"e2158d5c-ecdb-4b0f-bc3e-4ab632429de3"}],"links":[["reverence","reverence"]],"categories":["English terms with quotations"],"glosses":["A feeling of fear and reverence."],"tags":["uncountable","usually"],"id":"480180a4-804e-461d-a9b4-1b0515cb8f73"},{"examples":[{"text":"For several minutes no one spoke; I think they must each have been as overcome by awe as was I. All about us was a flora and fauna as strange and wonderful to us as might have been those upon a distant planet had we suddenly been miraculously transported through ether to an unknown world.","ref":"1918 September–November, Edgar Rice Burroughs, “The Land That Time Forgot”, in The Blue Book Magazine, Chicago, Ill.: Story-press Corp., →OCLC; republished as chapter IV, in Hugo Gernsback, editor, Amazing Stories, (please specify |part=I to III), New York, N.Y.: Experimenter Publishing, 1927, →OCLC:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[82,85]],"id":"c7634f97-d713-43d6-8b1d-04f3d22a0347"},{"text":"In 1825, the first public railway carried passengers across the English countryside, setting in motion not just an engineering revolution, but an industrial one too. Imagine the awe and excitement of those first passengers as they boarded the train, unaware that they were witnessing the dawn of a new era.","ref":"2025 October 1, Richard Evans, “The value of the railway effect”, in RAIL, number 1045, page 58:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[178,181]],"id":"29bd80e9-8b8a-4f23-bbf6-b2d9bc42aa47"}],"categories":["English terms with quotations"],"glosses":["A feeling of amazement."],"tags":["uncountable","usually"],"id":"5647c419-733f-42dc-900b-7c4f24cd51d5"},{"categories":["English terms with archaic senses"],"links":[["awe","awe"]],"raw_glosses":["(archaic) Power to inspire awe."],"glosses":["Power to inspire awe."],"tags":["archaic","uncountable","usually"],"id":"3bc812ec-dd7a-46c5-8922-6610fd8aec0a"}],"related":[],"synonyms":[]},"awestruck":{"id":"031855d5-f3fc-439a-a904-914c01c45e8f","word":"awestruck","trans":[{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"filled or overcome with awe","word":"deslumbrado"}],"pos":"adj","tags":null,"senses":[{"examples":[{"text":"Like so many others, I was awestruck by the first season, which captured a moment in time and successfully funnelled its rage outwards at a world in which women are indeed silenced, controlled and killed by men.","ref":"2018 June 16, Fiona Sturges, “Cattleprods! Severed tongues! Torture porn! Why I’ve stopped watching the Handmaid’s Tale”, in Katharine Viner, editor, The Guardian, London: Guardian News & Media, →ISSN, →OCLC, archived from the original on 05 Feb 2020:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[27,36]],"id":"77b34268-3840-45df-97ac-0a54fbd3415a"}],"links":[["Filled","fill#Verb"],["overcome","overcome"],["awe","awe"],["wonder","wonder#Noun"]],"synonyms":[{"word":"awestricken"}],"categories":["English adjectives","English compound terms","English entries with incorrect language header","English lemmas","English terms derived from Proto-Indo-European","English terms derived from the Proto-Indo-European root *h₂egʰ-","English terms with quotations","Entries with translation boxes","Pages with 1 entry","Pages with entries","Terms with Bulgarian translations","Terms with Esperanto translations","Terms with Finnish translations","Terms with French translations","Terms with German translations","Terms with Polish translations","Terms with Portuguese translations","Terms with Romanian translations","Terms with Spanish translations"],"glosses":["Filled or overcome with awe or wonder."],"id":"80fd00d4-6419-48c0-b3a9-5723f8c0e0fc"}],"related":[{"word":"awestrike"},{"word":"awestriking"},{"word":"thunderstruck"},{"word":"horror-struck"}],"synonyms":[]},"awesome":{"id":"43576c41-00ae-4b0c-aa3b-e59de637db89","word":"awesome","trans":[{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"causing awe or terror","word":"apavorante"},{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"causing awe or terror","word":"aterrador"},{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"excellent, exciting","word":"incrível"}],"pos":"adj","tags":null,"senses":[{"examples":[{"text":"The waterfall in the middle of the rainforest was an awesome sight.","bold_text_offsets":[[53,60]],"type":"example","id":"b3b5b7e1-a70d-454d-9104-fb287a511e04"},{"text":"The tsunami was awesome in its destructive power.","bold_text_offsets":[[16,23]],"type":"example","id":"efff6ffe-a93d-44a8-8658-bafef589a15e"},{"text":"And now it appeared that there was a mysterious Queen clothed by rumour with dread and wonderful attributes, and commonly known by the impersonal, but, to my mind, rather awesome title of She.","ref":"1886 October – 1887 January, H[enry] Rider Haggard, She: A History of Adventure, London: Longmans, Green, and Co., published 1887, →OCLC:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[171,178]],"id":"580bdc19-4fd0-45c5-8322-ab483d736a64"},{"text":"I think that the most fearsome attribute of these awesome creatures is their silence and the fact that one never sees them—nothing but those baleful eyes glaring unblinkingly out of the dark void behind.","ref":"1913 January–May, Edgar Rice Burroughs, “The Gods of Mars”, in The All-Story, New York, N.Y.: Frank A. Munsey Co., →OCLC; republished as “The Eyes in the Dark”, in The Gods of Mars, Chicago, Ill.: A[lexander] C[aldwell] McClurg & Co., September 1918, →OCLC, page 227:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[50,57]],"id":"4ce7cd3c-4c78-48e6-8c66-670069612573"},{"text":"Certainly it is awesome to think of a nation that brings its powers of persuasion against a woman's right to conceive.","ref":"1984 February 14, John Corry, “Birth Curb in China”, in The New York Times, →ISSN:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[16,23]],"id":"c0008ae0-361e-4ae2-876e-1f51475ba3fe"},{"text":"“Congratulations, President Trump,” Netanyahu said in a video statement immediately following the U.S. attack. “Your bold decision to target Iran's nuclear facilities with the awesome and righteous might of the United States will change history.”","ref":"2025 June 25, Daniel Estrin, quoting Benjamin Netanyahu, “Israel was once deterred from striking Iran. Now Netanyahu takes a victory lap”, in NPR:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[176,183]],"id":"e76dcb4a-c116-4e20-8000-47ac5e44ae03"}],"attestations":[{"date":"from 1590–1600.","references":[]}],"links":[["awe","awe"],["terror","terror"],["inspiring","inspire"],["wonder","wonder"],["excitement","excitement"]],"synonyms":[{"word":"awe-inspiring"}],"antonyms":[{"word":"aweless"}],"categories":["English terms with quotations","English terms with usage examples"],"glosses":["Causing awe or terror; inspiring wonder or excitement."],"id":"41bc88b2-0d66-4372-b1e6-4c42f0a12382"},{"examples":[{"text":"That was awesome!","bold_text_offsets":[[9,16]],"type":"example","id":"4822ff2e-85d3-4335-b58c-7b8b8e851504"},{"text":"Awesome, dude!","bold_text_offsets":[[0,7]],"type":"example","id":"37610f6e-2009-4236-90fc-fd0bec3801c8"},{"text":"Awesome! Totally awesome! All right, Hamilton!","ref":"1982, Cameron Crowe, Fast Times at Ridgemont High, spoken by Jeff Spicoli (Sean Penn):","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[0,7],[17,24]],"id":"1f0f7586-3408-4f9f-b8b7-d97fc2585e8d"}],"categories":["American English","Australian English","Canadian English","English colloquialisms","English terms with quotations","English terms with usage examples"],"links":[["Canada","Canada"],["US","American English"],["Excellent","excellent"],["exciting","exciting"],["remarkable","remarkable"]],"synonyms":[{"word":"ace","source":"Thesaurus:excellent","tags":["Britain","slang"]},{"word":"admirable","source":"Thesaurus:excellent"},{"word":"amazing","source":"Thesaurus:excellent"},{"word":"awe-inspiring","source":"Thesaurus:excellent"},{"word":"awesome","source":"Thesaurus:excellent","tags":["colloquial"]},{"word":"badass","source":"Thesaurus:excellent"},{"word":"bang on","source":"Thesaurus:excellent"},{"word":"bang-up","source":"Thesaurus:excellent"},{"word":"studly","source":"Thesaurus:excellent"},{"word":"based","source":"Thesaurus:excellent"},{"word":"beatific","source":"Thesaurus:excellent"},{"word":"beneship","source":"Thesaurus:excellent"},{"word":"bitching","source":"Thesaurus:excellent","tags":["slang"]},{"word":"blissful","source":"Thesaurus:excellent"},{"word":"bomb","source":"Thesaurus:excellent","tags":["slang"]},{"word":"brilliant","source":"Thesaurus:excellent"},{"word":"bully","source":"Thesaurus:excellent"},{"word":"celestial","source":"Thesaurus:excellent"},{"word":"cher","source":"Thesaurus:excellent","tags":["New-Zealand"]},{"word":"choice","source":"Thesaurus:excellent"},{"word":"chronic","source":"Thesaurus:excellent","tags":["slang"]},{"word":"chur","source":"Thesaurus:excellent","tags":["New-Zealand"]},{"word":"cock on","source":"Thesaurus:excellent"},{"word":"commendable","source":"Thesaurus:excellent"},{"word":"cool","source":"Thesaurus:excellent","tags":["slang"]},{"word":"copacetic","source"